1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,860
 And please, we welcome your questions tonight.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,400
 Thank you.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,660
 Thank you very much, Mr. McQueen.

4
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:07,140
 Mr. Theodore Rescoe.

5
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:08,040
 Thank you, Ms. La Mairese.

6
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:08,680
 Hi, everybody.

7
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,800
 Good to be back after the summer break.

8
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,140
 Happy to see our colleague, Peter McQueen, back on stage with us.

9
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:18,940
 .

10
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:21,220
 So a few files that I'd like to follow up

11
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,120
 on the stuff that we did at the borough level

12
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,580
 in the past few months.

13
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:29,280
 One, and I'm particularly proud to say that we're moving ahead.

14
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:32,100
 After 30 years of inaction from past administration

15
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,300
 is the Empress Project.

16
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,100
 As you know, there has been a public consultation.

17
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:37,980
 It's still going on.

18
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:41,380
 And we're going to talk about democracy later in the motion.

19
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,960
 And this is just one example of all the different ways

20
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:47,020
 that we can actually consult with the population.

21
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:50,160
 And one that is going on now until the 20th of September

22
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:54,080
 is the online survey that you can access through the website.

23
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:58,560
 And also, we've been with our population on the streets

24
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,380
 at Imagine Monkland to collect more

25
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:05,820
 than about 100 responses of what should happen there

26
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:08,200
 during the transition phase.

27
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:13,020
 Don't forget, there is a big consultation evening happening at the Parc du Chalet,

28
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:20,620
 Le Rendez-vous, in Parc NDG, in front of the Empress, on the 14th of September at 7:00 PM.

29
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,020
 So show up early and in numbers.

30
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:27,840
 Just to let you know, we're still talking about the transition phase of this project.

31
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,660
 This is by no means the final destination.

32
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:33,480
 But this will be a way that we can move ahead.

33
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:36,300
 Like we said, manger l'éléphant une bouchée à la fois.

34
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:38,300
 Can we say that in English?

35
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:39,300
 Eat the elephant one?

36
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,300
 Okay.

37
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:44,300
 And so we're very proud to say that we're moving ahead.

38
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:50,300
 The second major project that we've polarized, mobilized, and really occupied our minds

39
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:54,300
 since we got into office is, in particular, la piste cyclable Terrebonne.

40
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:58,160
 And I know people are laughing, people are angry.

41
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:03,260
 It left no one, especially in Loyola, indifferent on the topic, right?

42
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:09,960
 So I don't think there's one topic that has been more present on the agenda every week,

43
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:12,940
 at every statutory meeting that we have with the services.

44
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:17,160
 It's really impressive, the amount of energy that we spend on this,

45
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,160
 because we know it's important.

46
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:22,000
 It's something that we heard loud and clear when we were doing the campaign.

47
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,080
 It's something that we took very seriously from day one.

48
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:30,740
 Since day one, we've looked at a dozen or more of scenarios.

49
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:36,100
 Some of you maybe have seen me, even recently, like a weirdo with my tape,

50
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:41,260
 measuring tape on different parts of the biking path in our borough

51
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:45,920
 and across the city, actually, to see precedents and comparables.

52
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:46,860
 You've seen me, right?

53
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:47,460
 You saw me?

54
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,640
 Yeah, okay.

55
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,320
 It's always me.

56
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:55,920
 Just to give us the range of possibilities and options, and again, the objective here,

57
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:03,280
 there is a path that is clear in front of me that we need to find a way to basically find

58
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:07,800
 a meeting ground for people who need more access with their cars, for their parking,

59
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:14,440
 for their needs, accessibility needs, and also preserve safety capacity for active mobility,

60
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,240
 for our families especially.

61
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:22,920
 So in the next couple of days, we will have an update, because it's now at the final stage of the study

62
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:29,240
 that we submitted recently with the services, and the services have promised us a final answer in the next few days.

63
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:37,160
 So before the end of fall, you will have our own orientation on what's going to happen this winter with the Terrebonne bike path.

64
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:41,720
 So it's coming.

65
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:48,280
 Another major project that I'm very proud of is, in terms of housing, especially vulnerable populations, right?

66
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:57,720
 And we all have to do our part, and I'm very happy that we've been included in the pilot project of 54 transitory units for women,

67
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:03,600
 des femmes vulnérables, and it's going to happen in my district of Loyola, in the West Haven community.

68
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:10,280
 And this was done, I'm very proud of this project, because the speed and the cost which are key to really solve,

69
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:15,560
 trying to put a dent in this massive housing shortage and affordability crisis that we have,

70
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:18,840
 this is one way of trying to tackle the issue.

71
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:24,360
 And so 54 units are coming up in the next few months in this community,

72
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,800
 and I think we can all be very, very proud of that achievement.

73
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:30,360
 So again, something to follow up on very, very soon.

74
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:37,480
 Just in terms of multitude of points, I've had a privilege,

75
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:42,360
 j'ai le privilège franchement d'assister à des événements fantastiques de la communauté pendant l'été, on peut le faire.

76
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,480
 J'ai assisté au festival interculturel de NDG.

77
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:49,080
 Merci à votre équipe fantastique, Hala, pour l'organisation.

78
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,640
 C'était fantastique de voir toutes ces différentes communautés,

79
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:55,000
 puis c'est vraiment la richesse, une des richesses de notre communauté à Côte d'Enege NDG.

80
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,080
 On le dit, on est très fiers de notre diversité.

81
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,000
 Strength is in our diversity.

82
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:04,000
 Et vraiment, j'ai eu un moment un peu émotionnel, parce que quand je voyais tous ces gens qui viennent de partout dans le monde,

83
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,720
 alors que quand on regarde les médias sociaux, quand on regarde les médias de partout,

84
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:11,560
 on a tendance à… les gens veulent nous mettre les uns contre les autres.

85
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:16,840
 Et là, j'ai trouvé un moment de bonheur où tout le monde, les moins âgés, les plus âgés,

86
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:22,040
 et de tous les horizons, de toutes les couleurs, étaient ensemble pour célébrer la force de notre communauté.

87
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,320
 J'en étais très fier.

88
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,200
 Et ça s'est reproduit aussi durant Imagine Monkland,

89
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:30,560
 durant Patrimoine, en fait, où on a mis de l'avant le 150e anniversaire de NDG.

90
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,920
 J'en étais très fier aussi.

91
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,920
 Et voilà.

92
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,920
 Je vais finir là-dessus.

93
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:38,800
 Mais jeunesse Loyola, s'il vous plaît, je suis allé les voir.

94
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,960
 Ils ont besoin de notre aide.

95
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,640
 C'est le moment de nous montrer notre générosité comme communauté.

96
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:46,960
 Ce qu'elle fait, Christine, avec ses 500 enfants, c'est du miracle.

97
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:50,040
 Alors, si on est tous là en train de se dire qu'on a beaucoup de problèmes dans la vie,

98
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:53,680
 allez lui parler à Christine Richardson et regardez comment vous pouvez l'aider, elle,

99
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,680
 à aider nos enfants de nos communautés.

100
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,960
 Je vous remercie.

101
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,120
 Merci beaucoup, Monsieur Théodoresco.

102
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:03,000
 Donc, tel qu'a demandé dans l'ordre du jour, nous allons directement

